          "factManual": false,
          "membershipEvidence": "Intel, Oracle, IBM, and quantum computing firm IonQ are the latest companies to object to having their shares traded on OKXICE TSV, according to an updated public notice from the venue dated Monday.\nThe venue is set to operate under the SEC’s innovation exemption, which the agency unveiled in September after the Clarity Act stalled in the Senate.\nUsers must pass identity and sanctions checks and hold a nontransferable “soulbound” token to trade.\nThe notice also says trades must be fully funded, with no margin or borrowing.\nit’s uncertain whether tokenized shares in a self-custodied wallet would count as customer property or be covered by the Securities Investor Protection Corporation",
